// Tests the fixed-point macros (hex.fixed_mul, hex.fixed_mul_low, hex.fixed_div), hex.mul_low and hex.mul_const.
// Signed Q-format edge values (0, the smallest step, +-1.0, +-0.5, the most negative / positive, -eps) at every
//   pairing, random values, and division by zero. Expected values are python's (seed 20261024):
//   fixed_mul = floor((a * b) / 16^f), fixed_div = (a * 16^f) / b truncated toward zero, both modulo 16^n.
// Each check prints '=' when the result is right. Every result starts as garbage.
stl.startup

GARBAGE = 0x5a3c96e15a3c96e15a3c96e15a3c96e1

// n=2, f=1
test_fixed_mul 2, 1, 0x0, 0x0, 0x0
test_fixed_div_by_zero 2, 1, 0x0
test_fixed_mul 2, 1, 0x0, 0x1, 0x0
test_fixed_div 2, 1, 0x0, 0x1, 0x0
test_fixed_mul 2, 1, 0x0, 0x10, 0x0
test_fixed_div 2, 1, 0x0, 0x10, 0x0
